          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.152,
            0.884,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Carry out the following subtractions using Brahmagupta’s method: a. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 8 } { 1 5 }   -   \\frac { 3 } { 1 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " b. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 2 } { 5 }   -   \\frac { 4 } { 1 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " c. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { 5 } { 6 } } - { \\frac { 4 } { 9 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " d. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 2 } { 3 } - \\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.221,
            0.719,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Subtract as indicated: a. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 3 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " from "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 0 } { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " b. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 8 } { 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " from "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 2 3 } { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " c. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 2 9 } { 7 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " from "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 4 5 } { 7 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.289,
            0.529,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Solve the following problems:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.32,
            0.885,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "a. Jaya’s school is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 7 } { 1 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " km from her home. She takes an auto for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " km from her home daily, and then walks the remaining distance to reach her school. How much does she walk daily to reach the school?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.442,
            0.884,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "b. Jeevika takes "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 0 } { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " minutes to take a complete round of the park and her friend Namit takes "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{13}{4}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " minutes to do the same. Who takes less time and by how much?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.535,
            0.487,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.9 A Pinch of History"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.575,
            0.885,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you know what a fraction was called in ancient India? It was called bhinna in Sanskrit, which means ‘broken’. It was also called bhaga or ansha meaning ‘part’ or ‘piece’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.646,
            0.887,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The way we write fractions today, globally, originated in India. In ancient Indian mathematical texts, such as the Bakshali manuscript (from around the year 300 CE), when they wanted to write "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " they wrote it as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " which is indeed very similar to the way we write it today! This method of writing and working with fractions continued to be used in India for the next several centuries, including by Aryabhata (499 CE), Brahmagupta (628 CE), Sridharacharya (c. 750 CE), and Mahaviracharya (c. 850 CE), among others. The line segment between the numerator and denominator in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\epsilon } { 2 } ^ { \\flat }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and in other"
            }
          ]
        },
